            "notes": "## Items\n\nIn Round 2, you really just want to build for [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) and there's a lot of flexibility. Depending on how much Stadium Cash you've earned you could go straight into debuffs. In that case, get either [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) or [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98). I usually go for [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) first, as it's cheaper and massively shuts down comps with high amounts of sustain, but you can really go either way. However, these items are expensive and if you don't have a lot of Stadium Cash or you don't feel like the debuffs are worth the Stadium Cash just yet, go for some cheap items that give a whole bunch of [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) instead. Examples include [Custom Stock](item_17d633af-8bcc-4893-b865-be0a7bc66fe2), [Energized Bracers](item_f83a1d9e-91f8-4d2c-bd62-c673b8d9fd2e) and [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56). I like [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) and its [Cooldown Reduction](stat_cooldown_reduction) a lot, as it'll help with both of Moira's cooldowns. A lower Fade cooldown can in turn help with putting out more [Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb) orbs. [Smart Orbs](item_47f5985c-9b63-40d2-938b-63a22154b9be) is also great, but I usually save it for when I have at least one of the debuff items.\n\nTip: Items like [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6) and [Champion's Kit](item_8682f8c7-8811-439b-8d50-fa81cd43ddce) are not at all cost-effective and should generally be avoided in the early rounds. Only use them when your item slots would be full otherwise. For example, [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6) gives 20% [Ability Power](stat_ability_power) and costs 6,000 Stadium Cash. In its place you could get [Power Playbook](item_6d8803cf-baa7-46ee-af91-51e7f2301418) and [Custom Stock](item_17d633af-8bcc-4893-b865-be0a7bc66fe2) for 20% [Ability Power](stat_ability_power), 10 health and 5% [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) instead, which only costs you 4,750 Stadium Cash. On top of that, unlike most Epic items, [Champion's Kit](item_8682f8c7-8811-439b-8d50-fa81cd43ddce) does not offer any sort of utility.",
