            "created_at": "2025-08-29T13:29:24.406155+00:00",
            "notes": "This is the final build, but there's a ton of flexibility depending on your own preferences and playstyle.\n\n## Power\n\nThe final power is entirely up to you. I think [Chain Grasp](item_17b85f3e-1b10-410d-8e02-c7ff61f502a0) is a decent option if you're more focused on doing damage. [Optimal Overflow](item_9d85ca48-b27a-435a-8ef9-247440e0f97d) on the other hand is a great option if you're healing a majority of the time, though I think this power works best in combination with a bunch of [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed) to activate it faster, so an item like [Alternative Energy](item_c3e816b3-9c39-4528-9578-e3fa610b6cc6) works well with it. [Voidhoppers](item_d4ce0c76-2500-40d6-b066-dca303be097f) can be great if you need a cleanse for any negative effects that are bothering your team, such as [Ashe](hero_37b42a2d-a82d-4a22-9df2-4c812c873b54)'s dynamite or [Ana](hero_f1aee6cf-704f-455f-a100-ec882ebbe000)'s anti-heal. This power also grants your allies Overhealth equal to 20% of your max Life, which should be quite a lot by Round 7, as your health scales with the amount of Stadium Cash you have. [Destruction\u2019s Divide](item_cb7be5fa-0098-4a3c-bf62-efb3738a97e6) is a great option if you want your ult to be more impactful, but do keep in mind that this power does nothing for you outside of your ult. [Catalytic Crystal](item_3e3f4f77-cdf8-4dda-a5b0-2fb9390aefc4) is a good choice when using this power. [Ethereal Excision](item_a2359da3-1aa5-406f-a82f-4a0bd66266ac) is another power to consider if you're more damage-focused, but I feel is more suited to Weapon or Survival builds. Another thing I want to note is that from my limited testing in the Practice Range, [Deconstruction](item_cc8c46cc-b4a3-4c0f-aeb6-f7837e0e8e7c) does not seem to work with [Moira](hero_7fb6ff1e-a193-40c0-bd0a-25c1928fbaed)'s orbs, so I would avoid this one in an orb build. My personal preference is for [Chain Grasp](item_17b85f3e-1b10-410d-8e02-c7ff61f502a0) and [Voidhoppers](item_d4ce0c76-2500-40d6-b066-dca303be097f).\n\n## Items\n\nAs for items, you should be able to afford [Extendrils](item_138e73a2-6915-4ffc-bd89-029a85bf94b8) now. [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505), [Liquid Nitrogen](item_a8d99526-05a3-4405-babb-b025479b1b98), [Extendrils](item_138e73a2-6915-4ffc-bd89-029a85bf94b8) and [Smart Orbs](item_47f5985c-9b63-40d2-938b-63a22154b9be) are essential in any debuff orb build in my opinion. [Extendrils](item_138e73a2-6915-4ffc-bd89-029a85bf94b8) in combination with [Smart Orbs](item_47f5985c-9b63-40d2-938b-63a22154b9be) will make your debuffs constant. The reason why I don't usually go for [Extendrils](item_138e73a2-6915-4ffc-bd89-029a85bf94b8) earlier on is because it's not very cost-effective, especially compared to something like [Smart Orbs](item_47f5985c-9b63-40d2-938b-63a22154b9be). [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) and [Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e) could be replaced with any of the optional items listed, depending on your personal preferences or Stadium Cash, but I think both items have a rightful place in a debuff orb build. [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) gives some great survivability and has syngergy with [Phantasm](item_21ed9c3d-7a54-438f-9188-f21fd7a7dbfb) and [Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e) helps put out a ton more debuff orbs.",
